OneiOS, stack 555b13d (NativeMetal 935c468), patches-555b13d/NativeMetal/0010: an opt-in bounded wait for pipelines being
made, for the first-use compile stutters.
Upstream: none (OneiOS). The policy is metal2vulkan's own default (crates/metal2vulkan/src/device/policy.rs:
PipelineWaitPolicy::Bounded with pipeline_creation_wait and pipeline_commit_wait, 4.5 s each; in 624bab3 and 555b13d alike);
NativeMetal's bridge replaces it with Exact, as Metal compiles inside newRenderPipelineState.
What: with ONEIOS_PIPELINE_WAIT_MS=N (1..4500) the device is opened with Bounded and N ms for both waits. Read in
555b13d (pipeline/render.rs settle_graphics_pipeline and make_at_creation): under Exact the creation makes the pipeline on the
calling thread before it returns; under Bounded it hands the making to the runtime's pool and waits N ms at most, and a
command buffer waits N ms after its commit at most, then records the draws and dispatches whose pipeline is still being
made as nothing (the runtime counts them and announces draw-dropped-still-making / dispatch-dropped-still-making); later
command buffers draw with the pipeline once made. The pool thread makes the driver's call itself
(METAL2VULKAN_COMPILE_ON_ASKING_THREAD stays as the plug-in set it: it only chooses between the calling thread and a relay
thread for the driver's call, device/compiles.rs at_user_initiated). Only on this pin: metal2vulkan later holds such draws
instead of dropping them (RUNTIME 2161, 11-12, after 555b13d), so the experiment must be read again at the next move.
Why: take19/take20: backboardd's first-ever pipelines are 17-120 ms compiles each, on the thread that draws the frame (284 in
take19's session: the shade, the keyboard, menus, the wallpaper gallery). With a wait of about half a frame the frame is
shown without what the new pipeline draws, which appears some frames later, instead of every frame waiting.
Risk (why off): what a new pipeline draws is missing while it compiles (a layer's blur, mask or backdrop popping in); the
bridge's authors chose Exact after the render server showed missing pieces of the screen under the 4.5 s default. An A/B
for the owner's eye, not a default.
Switch: boot argument oneios-pipeline-wait-ms=N (try 4): Switches-555b13d.inc sets ONEIOS_PIPELINE_WAIT_MS in backboardd
alone. OFF without it. Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=pipeline-wait-bounded-switch).
Tested: cargo check of the bridge for arm64e-apple-ios with it. Not run anywhere.

